# Root build context for images built with `docker build -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .`
# (today: mcp-hub, via build-mcp-hub.yml -- OPS-112, 2026-09-12).
#
# WHITELIST. Everything is excluded, then the trees an image may COPY are
# re-admitted. The list is the set of trees the R26.09 refactor plan names as
# image content: apps/mcp-hub itself, the dispatcher (M9: factory intake as a
# gateway capability), the substrate's client package (M6/M12), and scripts/
# (the shared client lives there until M6 moves it). Adding a tree here is an
# outer-loop change; a worker's bead scope never includes this file.
#
# Not applied to images whose context is their own directory
# (build-lifeops-console.yml builds apps/lifeops-console/ as before).
*
!apps/mcp-hub/pyproject.toml
!apps/mcp-hub/src/
!apps/factory-dispatcher/
!apps/substrate/
!scripts/
# ADDED 2026-09-17 (#909 gate, F1). file_task.py:61 derives REQUIREMENTS_DIR as
# parents[2]/docs/requirements, which is /app/docs/requirements in the image. Without
# this tree the gateway intake refuses every spec that CITES a real requirement while
# accepting every spec that WAIVES traceability -- and its reason text diverges from the
# CLI's, breaking the same-reason parity criterion. Only the registry is admitted, not
# docs/ at large.
!docs/requirements/
# Never image content, even inside an admitted tree.
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/node_modules/
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/tests/
**/*.pyc
apps/substrate/tests/
apps/factory-dispatcher/tasks/
apps/factory-dispatcher/tests/
